Hello,

on 01/06/04 22:10, ezra peisach wrote:
> If one moves to power state: S1 - the screen does not go blank (text
> remains) When power is restored, the machine accepts keyboard input,
> but the screen then goes blank.
I got a similar problem on 2.6.0 with no ACPI patch, while entering in
S3 with (and not S1): I've a clean resume, but the screen remains blank,
while keyboard inputs are accepted. I posted my problem here
>
http://sourceforge.net/mailarchive/forum.php?thread_id=3676335&forum_id=6102

Sleeping in S3 from an terminal in an X session doesn't restore the X
session, but starting the shutdown (always without seeing my typing),
restore tty1 showing normal messages on shutdown (like "Shutdown called
from..." and "acpi_power_off_called"), as usual when I press the
'power-button' from an X session.

I'm on an ASUS M3410C (M3N): http://luca.pca.it/projects/asus/m3410c.php
Attached my DSDT from 'cat /proc/acpi/dsdt > dsdt.raw'. Maybe it could
be useful.

Please excuse me if the problems aren't related.

Thx, bye,
Gismo / Luca
